<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_centering">
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Material 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p4.1" class="ltx_p">This supplementary material provides additional technical and implementation details, alongside extended experimental results and further analyses that complement the main paper.
Specifically, the material is organized as follows:</p>
<ul id="A0.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A0.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Datasets ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> provides details regarding the datasets.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Closed-world results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> extends the <em id="A0.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">closed-world</em> analysis from <a href="#S3.T1" title="In 3.1 Preliminaries ‣ 3 Closed-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (<span id="A0.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main</span>) by reporting granular, per-category performance breakdowns.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Open-world results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> presents the full set of results for the <em id="A0.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">open-world</em> setting (<a href="#S4.T2" title="In 4.4 Evaluation protocol ‣ 4 Open-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in <span id="A0.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main</span>), including evaluations on 4-shot and 8-shot configurations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Streaming results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> provides the complete data for the <em id="A0.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">streaming</em> experiments visualized in <a href="#S4.F6" title="In 4.6 Streaming ICL ‣ 4 Open-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> (<span id="A0.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Implementation details ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> outlines the implementation specifics.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Qualitative results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> showcases an extended gallery of qualitative examples, complementing the visualizations in <a href="#S4.F4" title="In 4.4 Evaluation protocol ‣ 4 Open-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (<span id="A0.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main</span>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Datasets</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize the evaluation datasets in <a href="#A2.T3" title="In Appendix B Closed-world results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
The experiments utilized the same training and test splits as previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Closed-world results</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents the detailed, per-dataset results of the experiments described in <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Are CLIP-like VLMs really better than LMMs? ‣ 3 Closed-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Secs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1 Preliminaries ‣ 3 Closed-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (<span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main</span>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As they did not fit on a single page, we split the table into two parts, showing contrastive VLMs in <a href="#A2.T4.st1" title="In Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Closed-world results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(a)</span></a> and generative LMMs in <a href="#A2.T5.st1" title="In Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Closed-world results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(a)</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For contrastive VLMs (<a href="#A2.T4.st1" title="In Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Closed-world results ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(a)</span></a>), we report the performance of the <span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Zero-Shot</span> model, Tip-Adapter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> using the same backbone, and k-NN (as described in <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Are CLIP-like VLMs really better than LMMs? ‣ 3 Closed-world classification ‣ Large Multimodal Models as General In-Context Classifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> in <span id="A2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main</span>).
For both Tip-Adapter and k-NN, we report results with 4, 8, and 16 shots.
For each experiment, we report the average (<span id="A2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Avg.</span>) on the ten datasets, and highlight the delta <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t.<span id="A2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span> the average of the corresponding <span id="A2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Zero-Shot</span> model.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Dataset details.<span id="A2.T3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Summary details of the datasets used in our experiments.</span></span></figcaption>
